{"resourceIdentifier":"3004","resourceName":"Ontario Sustainable Community (OSC)","description":"This group project is intended to stimulate and reward the Ontarian ICI building owners and operators (Industries, Commerce and Institution) – large or small – for their efforts to reduce GHG emissions, by providing access to the voluntary carbon credit markets and beyond any regulated compliance.  This group project, based under the VM0018 methodology, is designed to be simple, yet rigorous in its application, measurement, and monitoring. Even though the eligible activities vary, energy consumption and waste management, and eventually transportation, are similar across many companies and organizations. The main objectives are as follows: to gradually group inside a Sustainable Community or cluster, up to 50,000 Client Facilities (buildings), located inside the province of Ontario, Canada  that will achieve a potential of 50,278,000 tCO2e of reductions of GHG emissions for the period 2022-2028; to collect ground data in real-time, and consequently, stimulate and enhance Industrial Commercial and Institutional (ICI) buildings to have a better sustainable behaviour. This approach stimulates and rewards all the small actions carried out by each of the ICI sites: diverting industrial and commercial waste from landfills for more efficient waste recovery and increasing energy efficiency in buildings. Transportation efficiency improvements are under development and will be added during the project. This group project will impacts positively on the Sustainable Developments Goals (SDG); 9,10,11,12,13 and 17.  The philosophy of this group project is supported by our endorsement of the Carbon Core concept (CCP) produced in May 2021 by the TSVCM.","location":{"latitude":44.873753,"longitude":-101.186200},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2022-08-02","endExclusive":"2022-09-02","endInclusive":"2022-09-01"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","v